    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass. The change is implemented as a full-stack, additive change:\n\n- **Front-end** (`ClientsPage.tsx`): validates the email against a pattern on submit; if invalid it renders a `client-form-email-error` element and skips the POST, so no row is created. Also surfaces the error if the server rejects.\n- **Server** (`ClientsPostLogic.java`): re-validates the email and throws `HttpException(BAD_REQUEST)` for a blank/malformed address \u2014 defense in depth so the API can't be bypassed.\n- **Database** (`V2__clients_email_check.sql`): a new Flyway migration adding a `CHECK` constraint enforcing a well-formed email at the schema level.\n\nAll three checks share the same pattern (`local@domain.tld`, no spaces), and no existing `data-testid` values were renamed or removed \u2014 `client-form-email-error` matches exactly what the spec asserts.",
